  "body": "  For every rational datum in , the canonical sequence is strict exact, and is a strict surjection. Equivalently, The coefficient maps used in these identifications commute with rational restriction.   Lean (loc_row_exact)  Lean (loc_pair_isEmbedding)  Lean (locRhoC_surjective)  Lean (locRhoC_continuous)  Lean (locRhoC_isOpenMap)  Lean (presheafValueMapC_restriction)  Lean (presheafValueMapB_restriction)   By , all four ideals are closed. Hence gives The two exact rows and give algebraic exactness of .  Let be the image of in ; this is a ring of definition. Since is surjective, so is . Thus is a strict surjection.  It remains to check strictness at the left. Let have images in and . Choose representatives and . Their difference belongs to . Choose as in . There is with . Lift to . Then is a compatible pair in , so it comes from . Its class in is . Therefore which is the bounded-denominator criterion for strictness.  All maps used above come from the coefficient maps and . More generally, a homomorphism carrying a rational datum to induces a coefficientwise map which sends the relations for to those for . The pullback identifications therefore commute with these maps. Applying this to rational restriction, and then using presentation independence and transitivity, proves the asserted compatibility under refinement.   "
