  "number": "6.2",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  The Huber pair is sheafy.   Lean (isSheafy_JetA_of_dvr)  Lean (finiteJet_isSheafyFor_of_dvr)  Lean (finiteJet_isSheafyTateRing_of_dvr)  Lean (finiteJet_structurePresheaf_isSheafOfTopologicalRings_all_of_dvr)   Give their maximal rings of integral elements. The max\/Gauss estimates show that every structural map is norm-nonincreasing. Consequently it sends bounded subsets to bounded subsets; in particular, if is power-bounded, then the set of powers of its image is the image of the bounded set . The structural maps therefore send power-bounded elements to power-bounded elements and define morphisms of Huber pairs.  For a rational domain , its inverse image in each comparison spectrum is defined by the image of the same rational datum. By , the corresponding section rings form the natural exact sequence required in . Each of is an affinoid -algebra, hence is sheafy by Huber's theorem . The conclusion follows from .   "
