  "body": " Coefficientwise localisation   Let be a rational datum in , and put . There is a canonical topological algebra isomorphism It is natural for rational refinements represented in a finite head: if is the corresponding head restriction map, the induced restriction sends The same statement holds after increasing .    Let Since is affinoid, the ideal is closed and is strict; this is the degree-zero conclusion of . In particular, there is a constant such that every has a lift with .  By , Because the relations lie in the finite head, acts coefficientwise. Its image is exactly Indeed, the inclusion from left to right is immediate. Conversely, for a null family in , choose coefficientwise lifts with ; then is again a null family. Thus the corresponding ideal over is closed and as complete topological modules and as algebras. Since , this proves .  Every map used in is induced by the canonical quotient. If a further rational datum lies in the head, its first Koszul differential is again coefficientwise, so the same construction gives . Presentation independence and transitivity of rational localisation extend this compatibility to iterated refinements and to a larger finite head.   "
